Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: PiBridge
Source: https://github.com/artscout/PiBridge
Comment:
 PiBridge is a VR hub for Pimax headsets on Linux (not affiliated with Pimax).
 It contains code ported from omarchyvr (https://github.com/laughtt/omarchyvr),
 used under its MIT terms. See the NOTICE file for the full attribution of
 ported and third-party material.
 .
 Two components are BUNDLED because they are not distribution packages:
   * usr/lib/pibridge/steamvr-monado/  - the PiBridge Monado SteamVR driver, our
     build of the Monado fork vendored in third_party/monado/ (Boost Software
     License 1.0, as Monado). Shipped prebuilt and stripped.
   * usr/lib/pibridge/libonnxruntime.so* - Microsoft ONNX Runtime (MIT), required
     by the Pimax driver for Mercury hand tracking. Not packaged in Debian/Ubuntu.
 .
 Excluded on purpose (licence / not our code): the Mercury hand models, the
 Pimax Play DLLs and the windata kit, winbridge.exe build output, and the
 external lens/calibration data. Only repo content plus the two bundled
 components above are shipped.

